{"book":24,"chapter":41,"context":{"chapter":41,"title":"Murder at Mizpah","summary":"Ishmael, of the royal family, murders Gedaliah at a meal, kills the Judean and Babylonian soldiers with him, and slaughters pilgrims bringing offerings, throwing the bodies into an old cistern. Johanan pursues him and frees the captives, but fearing Babylon's revenge, the survivors head toward Egypt.","background":"Killing a host after sharing his bread was an especially shocking betrayal (Psalm 41:9). Ishmael was 'of the seed royal' (v. 1) and was backed by the king of Ammon (40:14). The cistern had been dug by King Asa when he fortified Mizpah (1 Kings 15:22). Jewish tradition still keeps the 'Fast of Gedaliah' in the seventh month.","customs":[{"term":"Beards shaven, clothes rent","verses":"41:5","note":"Signs of mourning. These pilgrims from the north were grieving the temple's destruction while still bringing offerings to its site."}],"watchFor":["Ishmael's false tears (v. 6).","Ten men bargain for their lives with hidden food stores (v. 8).","Fear of Babylon drives the next decision (v. 18)."],"connections":["2 Kings 25:25-26","1 Kings 15:22","Psalms 41:9","Zechariah 7:5"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["בַּחֹדֶשׁ","bachodesh","H2320","HRd/Ncmsa","in the month"],["הַשְּׁבִיעִי","hashevi'i","H7637","HTd/Aomsa","<the> seventh"],["בָּא","ba'","H935","HVqp3ms","he came"],["יִשְׁמָעֵאל","yishma'el","H3458","HNpm","Ishmael"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["נְתַנְיָה","netanyah","H5418","HNpm","Nethaniah"],["בֶן","ven-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["אֱלִישָׁמָע","'elishama'","H476","HNpm","Elishama"],["מִזֶּרַע","mizera'","H2233","HR/Ncmsc","one of [the] offspring of"],["הַמְּלוּכָה","hamelukhah","H4410","HTd/Ncfsa","<the> royalty"],["וְרַבֵּי","verabei","H7227","HC/Ncmpc","and [the] chiefs of"],["הַמֶּלֶךְ","hamelekh","H4428","HTd/Ncmsa","the king"],["וַעֲשָׂרָה","va'asarah","H6235","HC/Ncfsa","and ten"],["אֲנָשִׁים